0016> is also in <MATH_0017>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e0f2708d0daebe7f1dcd241f4a2396bd2306c949099afa5d0aa4e10442a5c6e2", "unit_id": "tag:001D:statement"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0013", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{A} \\subset \\mathcal{B}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{A}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{B}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{A} \\subset \\mathcal{B}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{B}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{B}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\Ob(\\mathcal{B})$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:5816a14c5141d396ce988dfdc28dd3400586a4c0e4f2d6575ee6dcf4509338a6", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ae62a4f9f0132b7d84f99efc908ee17247f0e2227043f6a4254c92bdbfef1266", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nIf <MATH_0001> is a subcategory then the\nidentity map is a functor from <MATH_0002> to <MATH_0003>.\nFurthermore a subcategory <MATH_0004>\nis full if and only if the inclusion functor is fully faithful.\nNote that given a category <MATH_0005> the set of full subcategories\nof <MATH_0006> is the same as the set of subsets of\n<MATH_0007>.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:61e8bca5e730a640a931dda29f2dd3769857a995c18d98e6f9e29466e662f583", "unit_id": "tag:0013:paragraph-0005"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "remark", "parent_tag": "0013", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{A}$", "MATH_0002": "$F$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{A}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\textit{Sets}$", "MATH_0005": "$F$", "MATH_0006": "$F(\\Ob(\\mathcal{A}))$", "MATH_0007": "$F$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{A}$", "MATH_0009": "$F(\\Ob(\\mathcal{A}))$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{sets-section-sets-everything}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{remark}\n\\label{remark-functor-into-sets}\n", "suffix": "\\end{remark}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e64a52f350c9be9c00e58701de533b99e4ec9b13f4c17e261ba31132e6624f50", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d8e173878c265d10159ac5b4c459e0393b960af312a9d9b1d2fc63250d0de740", "source_text": "Suppose that <MATH_0001> is a category.\nA functor <MATH_0002> from <MATH_0003> to <MATH_0004>\nis a mathematical object (i.e., it is a set not a class or a formula\nof set theory, see\nSets, Section <REF_0001>)\neven though the category of sets is ``big''.\nNamely, the range of <MATH_0005> on objects will be\na set <MATH_0006> and then we\nmay think of <MATH_0007> as a functor between\n<MATH_0008> and the full subcategory\nof the category of sets whose\nobjects are elements of <MATH_0009>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:2f53561c92680464e2b1b957540713203e3aaaa81b1f26475acd9b9f1c8f4898", "unit_id": "tag:001E:statement"}
